## THE DECISIONS INSIDE THIS LANE (each Tuesday's default as coordinator; each a Question at the stamp; each a behaviour with a cell)
- **D1 (F1: what "truly read-only" means; Q1).** Every public member of the emitted runtime and of the generated catalogue whose type is a generic read-only collection (`IReadOnlyList<T>`, `IReadOnlyCollection<T>`, `IEnumerable<T>`) returns an object that (a) is NOT an array, and (b) when it implements the non-generic `System.Collections.IList`, reports `IsReadOnly` true, so that a cast to `IList<T>` and a write throws `NotSupportedException`. The four members of F1 and their sources at `main` (MEASURED, `file:line` printed by program): `Oxpd2Schema.Properties` (`Oxpd2RuntimeText.cs:207`, `=> _properties`, the array of `:192`), `Oxpd2Schema.EnumValues` (`:237`, an init-only property holding the `string[]` made at `:262`), `Oxpd2InboundOperation.RequestContentTypes` (`:1075`, the `string[]` stored at `:1053`), `Oxpd2InboundCatalogue.Operations` (emitted by `Oxpd2Generator.cs:73-74` as `... Operations { get; } = new ...Oxpd2InboundOperation[]`). **Default form:** each object keeps its private array for its own use and exposes ONE wrapper made once (`System.Array.AsReadOnly(...)` or `new System.Collections.ObjectModel.ReadOnlyCollection<T>(...)`: both names exist in the drive-local reference pack, MEASURED), never a new wrapper per read; `HasEnumValue` (`:328-332`, which today casts `(string[])EnumValues` at `:330`) and the parser's walk read the private array, never the public wrapper; `RequestContentTypes` wraps a COPY of the array its constructor receives; the catalogue is emitted as `global::System.Array.AsReadOnly(new ...Oxpd2InboundOperation[] { ... })`. **NOT covered (named limit, Q1):** reflection into private fields; the values a parse BUILDS (a generated model's `IReadOnlyList<T>` property holds whatever the serializer made for that one value: per-value, not shared, not state a later parse reads).
- **D2 (F1: the cells; Q2).** Two cells. (i) **A reflection walk** (`ReadOnlyListTests.No_public_list_of_the_runtime_or_the_catalogue_is_writable`): it visits `Oxpd2InboundCatalogue.Operations`, every operation in it, and every `Oxpd2Schema` reachable from every operation's `RequestSchema` and from every generated model's static `Oxpd2Schema` member (through `Properties[i].Schema` and `Items`, each schema once), applies D1 (a) and (b) to every public property of the kind D1 names, and asserts the list of offenders is empty, printing in its failure message the declaring type and member name of each offender (never a value). It prints (in the assertion message on failure, and in STATUS from a probe) the count of schemas visited: **a count of 0 is a STOP.** Its control (`Control_the_walk_names_a_member_that_hands_out_an_array`) feeds the same check function a test-local object with one public `IReadOnlyList<string>` member backed by an array and asserts it is named. (ii) **The cast-and-write cell** (`ReadOnlyListTests.A_cast_and_write_cannot_change_a_later_parse`), the verdict's own case, ORDERED so that a red run can never change shared state: (1) `Inbound.Get("UsbAccessories POST /operationCallback")` with body `{}` is refused `MissingRequired` (record the path); (2) an IDENTITY write (element 0 written back to index 0) through a cast to `IList<T>` on each of the four members (the schema's `Properties`, a schema's `EnumValues` from any enum site, that operation's `RequestContentTypes`, the catalogue's `Operations`) must throw `NotSupportedException` (an identity write changes nothing even where it is accepted, so the red run against `main` fails HERE by assertion and corrupts nothing); (3) only then the verdict's write (element `i` replaced by a new `Oxpd2Property` with the same name and schema and `Required` false, for the first required property) must throw `NotSupportedException`; (4) the same body `{}` is refused `MissingRequired` at the SAME path as in (1). No value of a body is printed.
- **D3 (F2: the highest body limit; Q3).** `Oxpd2ParseLimits` refuses `maxBodyBytes` above `System.Array.MaxLength - 1` with `ArgumentOutOfRangeException` naming `maxBodyBytes` (the constructor today checks only `maxBodyBytes < 1`, `Oxpd2RuntimeText.cs:56`), and exposes that bound as `public static int HighestMaxBodyBytes { get; } = System.Array.MaxLength - 1;` (a get-only static property: its backing field is init-only, so `BoundaryTests.No_static_field_of_the_adapter_is_writable` still holds, DERIVED); the constructor's summary says so. Why this bound: `ReadBoundedAsync` allocates `limit + 1` bytes at most (`:904` and `:915`), and `System.Array.MaxLength` is "The maximum count of elements allowed in any array" (the reference pack's own summary, MEASURED); its value is printed by your probe in STATUS (UNMEASURED here). **`ReadBoundedAsync` is NOT changed** under the default: with the bound, `limit + 1` cannot pass `int.MaxValue` (DERIVED). **Cost:** a caller asking `int.MaxValue - 1` (which works on `main`, RELAYED) is now refused at construction: a behaviour change, named in FOR TUESDAY.
- **D4 (F2: the cells; Q4).** (i) `LimitTests.Limits_above_the_highest_body_size_are_refused_when_made`: `HighestMaxBodyBytes + 1`, `int.MaxValue - 1` and `int.MaxValue` each throw `ArgumentOutOfRangeException` whose `ParamName` is `maxBodyBytes`; `HighestMaxBodyBytes` itself and `1` are accepted; `0` and `-1` still refused (unchanged). (ii) `LimitTests.A_client_at_the_highest_body_limit_reads_a_small_answer` (the verdict's "add the edge to N14"): the first JSON-answer method of every one of the 16 clients, built with `new Oxpd2ParseLimits(Oxpd2ParseLimits.HighestMaxBodyBytes, 32)` through the generated two-argument constructor (`DeviceClient(HttpClient http, Oxpd2ParseLimits limits)`, `Generated/Device/DeviceClient.cs:22`, MEASURED as the shape) over the existing fake device, answers its minimal body with a value and no exception (the existing `ClientResponseTests` helpers are reused; how `Clients.New` passes limits is yours to extend inside the test project).
- **D5 (F3: the Unicode-length cell; Q5).** Added to `InboundShapeTests.N9_strings_arrays_and_objects_past_their_bounds_are_refused` (`InboundTests.cs:216`), for every string site N9 already visits (`SitesOf(...).Take(2)` at `:220`): where the site has `MaxLength` M, a string of exactly M astral characters (each one Unicode scalar value outside the basic plane, two UTF-16 units: the test uses U+1F600) is ACCEPTED and M + 1 of them is refused `OutOfRange` at the site's path; where the site has `MinLength` m of 2 or more, m astral characters are accepted and m - 1 are refused `OutOfRange`. **The astral strings are written as RAW UTF-8 (4 bytes each) into the body, not as `\u` escapes:** MEASURED at `main`, two inbound sites (`data` in `Generated/Targets/UsbAccessories/Oxpd2Schemas.cs:70` and `:220`) carry `maxLength` 90110, and 90110 escaped pairs are 1,081,320 bytes, over the default 1,048,576-byte limit (DERIVED arithmetic), so an escaped body would be refused `TooLarge`, not judged on its length; raw, 90110 x 4 = 360,440 bytes. Each astral row asserts, before it judges, that the body is at most `Oxpd2ParseLimits.Default.MaxBodyBytes` (a row whose body is over the limit fails by its own assertion, never silently passes). The minLength row kills m8 only where m is 2 or more (6 occurrences of `Oxpd2Schema.String(2, ` in `Generated/Targets`, MEASURED by `grep`; none larger); the maxLength row is the one that kills m8 at every bounded site.
- **D6 (F3: the mutant; Q6).** m8 is the verdict's own mutant: in `LengthCheck` (`Oxpd2RuntimeText.cs:581-603`) count every UTF-16 unit (the condition `!char.IsLowSurrogate(text[i])` at `:591` made always true). Regenerated, built and run, it must turn N9 RED by assertion on the astral maxLength row of at least one operation; undone and proved. Without this red, F3 is not closed.

